                                <li><strong>Meaning:</strong> Manzil tak. Final stop.</li>
                                <li><strong>Example:</strong> "I am walking <strong>to</strong> the library." <br><em>(Matlab: Meri manzil library hai. Main andar jaunga.)</em></li>
                                <li><strong>Focus:</strong> Arrival (Pahunchna).</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li class="mt-4"><strong class="text-white text-lg">TOWARD(S) ka use (The Direction):</strong>
                            <p class="text-sm mt-1 mb-2">Jab aap 'toward' ya 'towards' use karte hain, toh focus <strong class="text-[#2563EB]">Raaste ya Disha</strong> par hota hai. Manzil par pohochna zaroori nahi hai.</p>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-gray-400">
                                <li><strong>Meaning:</strong> Ki taraf. Ki disha mein.</li>
                                <li><strong>Example:</strong> "I am walking <strong>toward</strong> the library." <br><em>(Matlab: Main library ki disha mein jaa raha hu. Shayad main raste mein kisi coffee shop pe ruk jau, library ke andar na jau.)</em></li>
                                <li><strong>Focus:</strong> Progress & Orientation (Us disha mein badhna).</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                    </ul>

